{% assign lts_schedule = include.lts_schedule | default: site.data.learn_to_scull_schedule %}
{% assign cohort = include.cohort %}
{% assign program_number = cohort.name | default: page.lts_program_number | default: "[LTS#]" %}
{% assign session_dates = cohort.session_dates | default: page.session_dates %}
{% assign next_session = session_dates[2] | default: "[Day, Date, Time]" %}
{% assign instructors = cohort.coaches | default: page.instructors %}
{% assign public_site_url = site.url | append: site.baseurl %}
Hi {{ program_number }} Crew,<br><br>

Excellent work in Session 2! You successfully transitioned your rowing skills to the water.<br><br>

**Key Achievements from Session 2**<br>
*   Gained confidence in rowing in a narrow sculling shell.<br>
*   Developed basic boat control and balance.<br>
*   Mastered safe launching and landing procedures.<br><br>

**Preparing for Session 3: Learning How To Push**<br>
To prepare for our next session, where we’ll focus on power application and navigation, please review:<br><br>
1.  Video Resources for Session 3: Watch the [Session 3 Videos]({{ public_site_url }}/for-learners/technique/videos.html?filter=session3).<br>
2.  Review the [Session 3 Learning Guide]({{ public_site_url }}/for-learners/learning-journey/session-3.html).<br><br>

**Next Session: {{ next_session }}**<br>
We’ll be working on:<br>
*   Reviewing navigation principles and river traffic patterns.<br>
*   Developing effective leg drive and power application.<br>
*   Mastering boat control through turns and varying stroke pressure.<br>
*   Building confidence through continuous rowing.<br><br>

**Continue Your Rowing Journey**<br>
Learn more about continuing with sculling: [Trial and Continuation Guide]({{ public_site_url }}/for-learners/resources/open-sculling-program-details.html).<br>
The four-week Open Sculling trial for {{ program_number }} is {{ cohort.trial_dates | default: "[trial dates]" }} and is priced at {{ lts_schedule.trial_fee }} for rowers not already covered by the Open/Tech Summer Program or Full Season.<br>
*   {{ lts_schedule.open_tech_fee_exemption_note }}<br>
*   If you wish to take advantage of the trial and are not already covered by the Open/Tech Summer Program or Full Season, please review the registration options at the bottom of the [Learn to Scull Class page]({{ lts_schedule.registration_url }}).<br>
*   For rowers paying separate LTS continuation fees, Phase 2 covers sculling only (no sweep) and begins immediately after your Learn to Scull class.<br><br>

**If you missed the Thursday noon sign-up and still want to try to row next week:**<br>
1.  Pay the applicable LTS Phase 2 fee through the [Learn to Scull Class page]({{ lts_schedule.registration_url }}), unless you are already covered by Open/Tech season fees, and follow [the practice signup instructions]({{ public_site_url }}/for-learners/resources/open-sculling-program-details.html).<br>
2.  Please email your instructors so we can ask Tom Kraft, our Sculling Head Coach, to consider your late request — there is no guarantee of getting boated.<br><br>

**Reminders**<br>
*   Arrive 10 minutes early.<br>
*   Weather forecast: {{ page.weather_forecast | default: "[Weather forecast, e.g., Sunshine at 60-71°F, wind 5-7 mph]" }}<br>
*   Bring your water bottle and sun protection.<br><br>

Keep up the great work! Let us know if you have any questions.<br><br>

Best regards,<br><br>
{% include communication_templates/signature.liquid instructors=instructors lts_schedule=lts_schedule %}
